      <div type="clause" n="29.2a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 29.2a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 29.2a" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="563" ed="#liebermann"/>Per plegium uero dimittatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.h"/> ad diem disracionandi uel emendandi; et seisiatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.25"/> placitet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.i"/> et sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.26"/> pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="k" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.k"/> capitali<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.27"/> suo; et non ducatur hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.28"/> namium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.29"/> extra hundretum.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 563 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gegen Bürgschaft aber bleibe Verklagter frei bis zum Termin</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">but on giving surety the defendant is to remain free until the appointed day</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verklagter; <hi rend="italic">wiederholt</hi> 53, 3; 5. 61, 21; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 5, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The defendant; repeated 53, 3; 5. 61, 21; cf. 5, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.k" n="k" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">das Erscheinen des Beklagten gelte statt seines gepfändeten Stück Vieh, <hi rend="italic">d. h.</hi> hebe Pfand- und Bürgenpflicht auf</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the appearance of the defendant is to count in place of his distrained beast, i.e. it cancels the obligation of pledge and surety</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sais. <hi rend="italic">Lond stets</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sais. Lond throughout</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si <hi rend="italic">K Co; fehlt Or;</hi> sic <hi rend="italic">Wh</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si K Co; missing in Or; sic Wh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vom Corr. umgestellt</hi> s. c. <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> s. c. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">transposed by the corrector s. c. Sc; s. c. the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> mam <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from mam Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bürgschaft befreit von Pfändung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 14a), und Beklagter braucht nur nach Herausgabe des Abgepfändeten zu antworten; sonst hätte er die (von kanonischer <hi rend="italic">exceptio spolii</hi> beeinflusste) Einrede der Entwerung; <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. Pol Mai II 47; Maitland <hi rend="italic">Coll. papers</hi> I 332</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Surety frees from distraint (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 14a), and the defendant need answer only after restitution of what was distrained; otherwise he would have the plea of disseisin (influenced by the canonical <hi rend="italic">exceptio spolii</hi>); <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. Pol Mai II 47; Maitland <hi rend="italic">Coll. papers</hi> I 332</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-2a.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Als Missbrauch beklagt <hi rend="italic">chacier naam hors del hundred</hi> Mirror of justices V 1, 78 ed. Whitaker 164.—Am Rande spät: <hi rend="italic">Nota, districtiones</hi> [abgepfändete Fahrhabe] <hi rend="italic">non ducendas extra hundretum</hi>—<hi rend="italic">suo captali</hi>{27}—<hi rend="italic">hoc</hi>{28} fehlt Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">chacier naam hors del hundred</hi> is complained of as an abuse in Mirror of justices V 1, 78 ed. Whitaker 164. — In the margin, in a late hand: <hi rend="italic">Nota, districtiones</hi> [distrained chattels] <hi rend="italic">non ducendas extra hundretum</hi> — <hi rend="italic">suo captali</hi>{27} — <hi rend="italic">hoc</hi>{28} missing Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
